<% content_for :title, "Backup" %>
<%= render "admin/tabs" %>
<h1>Backup</h1>
<p class="page-intro">
  One zip with everything: every household, account, schedule, pet, place and photo
  (<%= pluralize(@counts[:people], "person") %>, <%= pluralize(@counts[:households], "household") %>,
  <%= pluralize(@counts[:photos], "photo") %>).
</p>

<div class="form-card">
  <h2><%= icon(:download) %> Download a backup</h2>
  <p>
    To move to a new server, set it up fresh and choose <strong>Restore a backup</strong> on its setup page
    instead of creating an account. Everyone signs in there with their usual email and password.
  </p>
  <ul class="backup-notes">
    <li>Passkeys keep working only if the new server has the same address.</li>
    <li>Secrets stay encrypted to this server, so on a new one two-step verification is turned off
      (people set it up again), the email password needs entering again in Settings, and each device
      turns notifications back on by opening the app.</li>
    <li>It holds everything the board knows. Keep it somewhere as safe as the server itself.</li>
  </ul>
  <%= form_with url: admin_backup_path, method: :post, data: { turbo: false } do |f| %>
    <div class="form-actions">
      <%= f.button type: "submit", class: "btn btn-primary" do %><%= icon_label(:download, "Download backup") %><% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
  <p><small>From a shell: <code>bin/rails backup:create</code> writes one into <code>storage/backups</code>.</small></p>
</div>

<%# Restore over everything here. Loud on purpose: it can't be taken back
    from this page, so it says what goes, takes a typed RESTORE, asks once
    more, and saves a backup of what's here first. %>
<section class="form-card danger-zone restore-over">
  <h2><%= icon(:upload) %> Restore a backup</h2>
  <div class="flash-alert" role="note">
    <%= icon(:alert_circle) %>
    <div>
      <p><strong>This overwrites the whole database.</strong> Every household, account, schedule, pet, place and
        photo on this server is replaced by what's in the backup. Anything added or changed since that backup
        was made is lost.</p>
      <p>You'll be signed out, and everyone signs in with the accounts from the backup.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <ul class="backup-notes">
    <li>A backup of everything here now is saved first, in <code>storage/backups</code> on the server
      (<code>before-restore-&hellip;.zip</code>), so you can put it back if this was a mistake.</li>
    <li>The zip is checked before anything changes. If it isn't a backup this app can read, nothing happens.</li>
  </ul>
  <%= form_with url: admin_backup_restore_path, method: :post, multipart: true,
                data: { turbo_confirm: "Overwrite everything on this server with this backup? Anything since it was made is lost." } do |f| %>
    <div class="form-field">
      <%= f.label :backup, "Backup zip" %>
      <%= f.file_field :backup, accept: ".zip,application/zip", required: true %>
    </div>
    <div class="form-field">
      <%= f.label :confirm, "Type #{Admin::BackupsController::CONFIRM} to confirm" %>
      <%= f.text_field :confirm, required: true, autocomplete: "off", autocapitalize: "characters", spellcheck: false,
                       pattern: Admin::BackupsController::CONFIRM, title: "Type #{Admin::BackupsController::CONFIRM}" %>
    </div>
    <div class="form-actions">
      <%= f.button type: "submit", class: "btn btn-danger" do %><%= icon_label(:upload, "Overwrite with this backup") %><% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</section>
